  "id": "wayang_golek_sunda",
  "name": "Wayang golek and kliningan (Sundanese salendro gamelan)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Sundanese rod-puppet theatre and its concert counterpart kliningan, both carried by gamelan salendro: rebab, kendang, saron, bonang, kenong, jengglong, goong, gambang and kecrek, with a pesinden singer. In wayang golek the dalang narrates, voices every character and cues the ensemble; through cassettes and broadcasts the Giri Harja dalang family of Jelekong, Bandung, dominated the form from the 1980s.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1980s wayang golek and kliningan, art Music, southeast Asian branch. pelog slendro inflected, solo with instrumental accompaniment, slendro near equidistant. gamelan foundational carved hardwood canonical javanese rebab, gamelan sundanese kendang indonesian, saron gamelan, bonang, kenong, kempul. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
